From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: texts for ERROR_VIRUS_INFECTED and ERROR_VIRUS_DELETED

FormatMessage has texts for ERROR_VIRUS_INFECTED (225) and ERROR_VIRUS_DELETED
(226), which SG Defender's on-execute check (9456) makes programs see.
---
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/winerror.mc
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/winerror.mc
@@ -858,6 +858,16 @@
 Language=ENU
 Machine type mismatch.
 .
+MessageId=225
+SymbolicName=ERROR_VIRUS_INFECTED
+Language=ENU
+Operation did not complete successfully because the file contains a virus or potentially unwanted software.
+.
+MessageId=226
+SymbolicName=ERROR_VIRUS_DELETED
+Language=ENU
+This file contains a virus or potentially unwanted software and cannot be opened. Due to the nature of this virus or potentially unwanted software, the file has been removed from this location.
+.
 MessageId=230
 SymbolicName=ERROR_BAD_PIPE
 Language=ENU
